# Discogs -> Kaggle monthly sync
#
# Runs every day at 06:00 server time. This is intentional, not a typo: the script checks
# state/published_months.json and exits in seconds if the current month is already
# published, so a daily run costs almost nothing on the days there's nothing to do. That
# removes the guesswork of picking a fixed "day of month" for when Discogs will have
# published - whenever it lands, this catches it within 24 hours instead of waiting for
# next month if a fixed day is missed.
#
# The real, rotating log is logs/sync.log, written directly by the script itself
# (discogs_kaggle_sync/logging_setup.py) - it keeps 14 days of history on its own, so
# nothing here should also append to that same path forever. The redirect below is only a
# crash-catch net for failures before Python's own logging even starts (e.g. the venv
# python isn't where this line says); `>` overwrites it each run instead of `>>` so it
# never grows unbounded, since anything worth keeping is already in logs/sync.log.
#
# Install with: crontab -e   (then paste the line below, adjusting paths)

0 6 * * * cd /path/to/Discogs_Kaggle_Sync && /path/to/venv/bin/python run_monthly_sync.py --work-dir ./work --kaggle-owner ofurkancoban > logs/cron-last-run.log 2>&1

# Optional: catch drift between "marked published" and "actually complete on Kaggle"
# (see fill_descriptions.py --audit) once a week.
0 7 * * 1 cd /path/to/Discogs_Kaggle_Sync && /path/to/venv/bin/python fill_descriptions.py --kaggle-owner ofurkancoban --audit > logs/cron-audit.log 2>&1
